<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Locrians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Locrians were an ancient Greek people of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, divided into the eastern Locrians facing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euboea">Euboea</a> and the Ozolian Locrians on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-corinth">Gulf of Corinth</a>, separated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dori">Doris</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocis">Phocis</a>. Colonists from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/locris">Locris</a> founded Locri Epizephyrii in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, whose lawgiver <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaleucus">Zaleucus</a> was credited with one of the earliest written Greek law codes. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homer">Homer</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajax-the-lesser">Ajax the Lesser</a> was their legendary leader at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troy">Troy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/locrians.jpg" alt="Locrians" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: original:Map_greek_sanctuaries-en.svg by Marsyas derivative work: MinisterForBadTimes (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Greek_southern_regions.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
